<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khorasan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khurasan, Khurasani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khorasan is a historical region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and adjoining parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, containing cities such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nishapur">Nishapur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merv">Merv</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a>. It was the launching ground of the Abbasid revolution against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> and the base from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> rose. Its frontier position made it contested ground for the Safavid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empires</a> as well.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khorasan.jpg" alt="Khorasan" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hairy Dude · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khorasan-Transoxiana-Khwarazm_nopaths.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
